   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the election law, in relation to the form of paper ballots and party emblems",
    "basePrintNo": "S8153",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8153-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§7-106, 7-122 & 7-104, El L",
    "lawSection": "Election Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S8153\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the election law, in relation to the form of paper\nballots and party emblems\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill amends and updates several sections of Article 7 of the\nelection law to define election day paper ballots that will be used\nwhen utilizing ballot scanners.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill amends section 7-106 of the election law to\ndefine \"election day paper ballots\" that will be used with ballot\nscanners and codifies the instructions that will appear on the ballot.\n\nSection 2 of the bill amends section 7-122(1) of the election law to\nconform, where possible, the instructions on absentee ballots that\nwill be counted by hand.\n\nSection 3 of the bill amends section 7-104 of the election law to\nremove the party emblem in the voting square to allow additional space\nfor the candidate's name. It also clarifies that the party emblem will\nappear at the head of the column or the beginning of the row depending\non the orientation of the ballot next to the extended hand.\n\nSection 4 of the bill amends section 7-122 (2), (3), (4), (5), (8),\n(9) and (10) of the election law to conform, where possible, the\ninstructions absentee ballots that will be counted by a central\nscanner and to clarify how all absentee ballots shall be mailed to the\nvoter. This section also repeals all the provisions related to punch\ncard ballots.\n\nSection 5 of the bill is the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe State of New York is scheduled to begin to use polling place\nballot scanners beginning with the Primary Election in September 2010\nin compliance with the federal Help America Vote Act and enabling\nstate legislation. This bill defines the \"election day paper ballots'\nthat will be used with the new ballot scanners and conforms the form\nof absentee ballots to the new Election Day paper ballots where\npossible. The bill continues the format for ballots that has been in\nplace in New York for many years except where the features of the new\nmachines warrant a change in language or substance. Most notably, the\nparty emblem will no longer appear in the voting square to allow\nadditional space for a candidate's name. The party emblem will\ncontinue to appear at the head of the column or the beginning of the\nrow depending on the orientation of the ballot.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNone.\n\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATION:\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis bill would take effect immediately.\n\n",
